From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:41:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Revert "PCI: host-common / dwc / qcom: L2 at shutdown"
 (pw 1195891 v7 1-3/3)

On the Pad 4 every s2idle now logs "qcom-pcie 1c00000.pcie: Timeout
waiting for L2 entry! LTSSM: 0x12" (3 of 3 cycles), which q90z never
did. qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq() calls dw_pcie_suspend_noirq(pci, false),
which only sends PME_Turn_Off when pci_host_common_d3cold_possible()
says D3cold is possible. 1/3 fixes that bus walk's early exit, so with
WCN7860 behind the port it now returns true and s2idle tries L2 entry,
which the link (LTSSM L1 idle, 0x12) does not reach on this platform.

Take the whole series out (1/3 changes the s2idle decision; 2/3 and
3/3 only matter together with it) and restore the q91 state of the five
files, including the build fix our FIXUP commit made to 3/3. To be
reported with the series review.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
